---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'section1', label: '1. Acceptance of Terms' },
  { id: 'section2', label: '2. Eligibility & Accounts' },
  { id: 'section3', label: '3. Your Content' },
  { id: 'section4', label: '4. Limited License' },
  { id: 'section5', label: '5. Prohibited Content' },
  { id: 'section6', label: '6. Third-Party Services' },
  { id: 'section7', label: '7. Disclaimers & Liability' },
  { id: 'section8', label: '8. Modifications & Law' },
  { id: 'section9', label: '9. General Provisions' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply when you use Rehearse."
  lead="Please read these Terms carefully before uploading any content or using any features."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="section1">
    <h2>1. Introduction & Acceptance of Terms</h2>
    <p>
      By accessing or using Rehearse, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please stop
      using the platform immediately.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms form a legally binding agreement between you and the platform operator. Please read them carefully
      before uploading any content or using any features.
    </p>
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="callout-title">Important</span>
      Continued use of the platform after any updates to these Terms constitutes your acceptance of the revised Terms.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="section2">
    <h2>2. Eligibility & Account Responsibilities</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 13 years of age (or the minimum age of digital consent in your country) to use this platform.
      By using it, you confirm that you meet this requirement.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your login credentials and for all activities that occur
      under your account. Notify us immediately if you suspect unauthorized access.
    </p>
    <p>You agree to provide accurate and current information when creating your account and to update it as necessary.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="section3">
    <h2>3. Your Content — Ownership & Responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      You retain full ownership of all files, data, media, and other content you upload to the platform ("Your Content").
      We do not claim any ownership rights over it.
    </p>
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="callout-title">Legal Responsibility</span>
      You are solely responsible for all content you upload. By uploading content, you confirm that you own the rights
      (including copyright for sheet music) or have obtained all necessary permissions.
    </div>
    <p>By uploading content, you confirm that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your content does not infringe any third party's copyright, trademark, or privacy rights</li>
      <li>Your content complies with all applicable laws in your jurisdiction</li>
      <li>We are not responsible for reviewing the legality or ownership of your uploaded content</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="section4">
    <h2>4. Limited License to the Platform</h2>
    <p>To operate the service, you grant us a limited, non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Host, store, and back up Your Content on our infrastructure (provided by Supabase)</li>
      <li>Display Your Content to you and to those you specifically authorize</li>
      <li>
        Process and transform Your Content solely as needed to deliver the service (e.g. converting sheet music to
        playable audio)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>This license terminates when you delete Your Content or close your account.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="section5">
    <h2>5. Prohibited Content & Moderation</h2>
    <p>
      You agree not to upload or transmit content that is unlawful, harmful, infringing, threatening, defamatory, or that
      contains malware.
    </p>
    <p>
      We reserve the right, but not the obligation, to review, remove, or restrict access to any content that we believe
      violates these Terms or exposes the platform to legal risk.
    </p>
    <p>We may suspend or permanently terminate your account for serious or repeated violations of these Terms.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="section6">
    <h2>6. Third-Party Services & Integrations</h2>
    <p>
      Rehearse integrates with third-party providers for services such as cloud storage (Supabase) and authentication
      (Apple/Google). These third parties operate under their own terms and privacy policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not responsible for the availability or content of third-party services. Your use of such integrations is at
      your own risk.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="section7">
    <h2>7. Disclaimers & Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="callout-title">Disclaimer</span>
      Rehearse is provided "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis, without warranties of any kind. Your use of the platform is
      at your own risk.
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="callout-title">Accuracy Notice</span>
      While we aim to provide accurate musical notation and analysis, the output generated by Rehearse may not be 100%
      precise. Actual musical data, interpretation, or notation may differ from the processed results due to limitations
      in input quality, formatting, or system processing.
    </div>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, the platform operator shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, or
      consequential damages resulting from your use of the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      In no event shall our total liability to you exceed the greater of: (a) total fees you have paid us in the past 12
      months, or (b) USD $50.00.
    </p>
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="callout-title">User Content Liability</span>
      We are not liable for any harm or loss resulting from content uploaded by you or other users. You assume full legal
      responsibility for Your Content.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="section8">
    <h2>8. Modifications & Governing Law</h2>
    <p>
      We reserve the right to modify or discontinue the platform at any time. We may update these Terms periodically and
      will notify you of material changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which the platform operator is based, without regard to
      its conflict-of-law provisions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="section9">
    <h2>9. General Provisions</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Entire Agreement:</strong> These Terms and our Privacy Policy constitute the entire agreement between you and
      Rehearse.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Severability:</strong> If any provision is found to be unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue
      in full force.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Contact:</strong> For questions about these Terms, please contact us at
      <strong><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></strong>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
